v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"the allies","kjv":"and against the help"}},{"chapterId":"jer-37","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"to help","kjv":"to help"}},{"chapterId":"lam-4","v":17,"renderings":{"bsb":"help","kjv":"help"}},{"chapterId":"nam-3","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"her allies"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Judges 5:23","note":"‘Curse Meroz,’ said Yahweh’s angel. ‘Curse bitterly its inhabitants, because they didn’t come to help Yahweh, to help Yahweh against the mighty.’","source":"web"},{"ref":"2 Chronicles 28:21","note":"For Ahaz took away a portion out of Yahweh’s house, and out of the house of the king and of the princes, and gave it to the king of Assyria; but it didn’t help…","source":"web"},{"ref":"Job 6:13","note":"Isn’t it that I have no help in me, That wisdom is driven quite from me?","source":"web"},{"ref":"Psalm 22:19","note":"But don’t be far off, Yahweh. You are my help. Hurry to help me!","source":"web"},{"ref":"Isaiah 10:3","note":"What will you do in the day of visitation, and in the desolation which will come from afar? To whom will you flee for help? Where will you leave your wealth?","source":"web"},{"ref":"Jeremiah 37:7","note":"“Yahweh, the God of Israel, says, ‘You shall tell the king of Judah, who sent you to me to inquire of me: “Behold, Pharaoh’s army, which has come out to help…","source":"web"},{"ref":"Lamentations 4:17","note":"Our eyes still fail, looking in vain for our help. In our watching we have watched for a nation that could not save.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Nahum 3:9","note":"Cush and Egypt were her boundless strength. Put and Libya were her helpers.","source":"web"}],"related":[],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}